  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CLARE - FCDO IDRC CLimate Adaptation and REsilience Framework Research Programme (CLARE)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CLARE is FCDO&apos;s flagship climate adaptation research programme. Run in collaboration with Canada&apos;s International Development Research Centre (IDRC) this component commissions new research that bridges critical gaps between science and action: developing tools, technology and evidence that support partner governments, communities and the private sector to drive effective solutions to the climate challenge, whilst strengthening capacity of both those carrying out the research and those using the resulting evidence. The first research call focuses on climate, humanitarian and socio-economic developmental issues across Africa and the Indo-Pacific, across three intersecting research themes: 1. empowering a better understanding of climate risks, 2. supporting early action to reduce impacts of climate variability whilst 3. enabling inclusive, climate-resilient development now and in the future.</narrative>
  </description>
